{
  "id": "nested-ifs",
  "title": "Nested Ifs",
  "reflection_prompt": "Nested ifs and combined conditions (from the next unit) can often solve the same problem. What made you reach for nesting instead of one big condition?",
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "01",
      "source_unit": "nested-ifs",
      "title": "Voting Eligibility with Registration",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "nested if",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read an <code>age</code>. If it's 18 or older, also read whether the",
        "person is registered (<code>yes</code> or <code>no</code>), and print",
        "<code>Can vote</code> or <code>Must register first</code> accordingly. If",
        "they're under 18, print <code>Too young to vote</code> without asking",
        "about registration at all.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "20",
        "yes",
        "Can vote</pre>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "16",
        "Too young to vote</pre>",
        "<p>Notice the second example only provides <strong>one</strong> line of",
        "input &mdash; the registration question should only be asked (and only",
        "read with <code>input()</code>) when the age check inside it is true. An",
        "<code>if</code> written inside another <code>if</code> like this is called",
        "a <strong>nested if</strong>.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "age = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: if age >= 18, read whether they're registered (\"yes\"/\"no\")",
        "# and print \"Can vote\" or \"Must register first\".",
        "# If age < 18, print \"Too young to vote\" (and don't ask about registration)."
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "20",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Can vote"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "20",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Must register first"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "16",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Too young to vote"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "18",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Must register first"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "17",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Too young to vote"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "02",
      "source_unit": "nested-ifs",
      "title": "Movie Ticket Discount",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "nested if",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read an <code>age</code>. If it's under 12, print",
        "<code>Child price</code>. Otherwise, also read whether they're a student",
        "(<code>yes</code>/<code>no</code>), and print <code>Student price</code> or",
        "<code>Regular price</code> accordingly.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "25",
        "yes",
        "Student price</pre>",
        "<p>This time the nested <code>if</code> lives inside the",
        "<code>else</code> branch, rather than inside the <code>if</code>.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "age = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: if age < 12, print \"Child price\".",
        "# Otherwise, read is_student (\"yes\"/\"no\") and print",
        "# \"Student price\" or \"Regular price\"."
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "8",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Child price"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "25",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Student price"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "25",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Regular price"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "11",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Child price"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "12",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Student price"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03",
      "source_unit": "nested-ifs",
      "title": "Password Strength Check",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "nested if",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read a password's <code>length</code> and whether it contains a number",
        "(<code>yes</code>/<code>no</code>). If the length is less than 8, print",
        "<code>Too short</code> &mdash; regardless of whether it has a number.",
        "Otherwise, print <code>Strong password</code> if it has a number, or",
        "<code>Weak password (no number)</code> if it doesn't.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "10",
        "yes",
        "Strong password</pre>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "length = int(input())",
        "has_number = input()",
        "",
        "# TODO: if length < 8, print \"Too short\".",
        "# Otherwise, print \"Strong password\" or \"Weak password (no number)\"",
        "# depending on has_number."
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "10",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Strong password"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "10",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Weak password (no number)"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Too short"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "8",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Strong password"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "7",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Too short"
        }
      ]
    },
